🚽 Test case: round-22 review finding #1's second regression -- a real
🚽 `skibidi`-declared function's return type is VAR_VOID now (round 20),
🚽 not NONE, but handle_return_statement()'s (ast.c) return-value switch
🚽 still only had `case NONE:` ("void/skibidi return type: ignore
🚽 expression value"), a comment left over from the pre-round-20 model
🚽 where `skibidi` meant NONE. An explicit `bussin 0;` inside a genuine
🚽 `skibidi` function reached that switch with type == VAR_VOID, missed
🚽 every case, and fell into `default: yyerror("Unsupported return
🚽 type"); exit(1);` -- a hard crash on an idiomatic, previously-working
🚽 pattern. `main` itself never hit this (it explicitly sets NONE, not
🚽 VAR_VOID, for "not inside any declared function"), which is why this
🚽 regression needed a REAL `skibidi`-declared function to surface at
🚽 all. Confirmed via a temporary A/B test (git stash to the pre-fix
🚽 commit) that this exact program exited 1 with "Unsupported return
🚽 type".
skibidi noop() {
    bussin 0;
}

skibidi main {
    noop();
    yapping("survived");
    bussin 0;
}
